 "notes": [
  "Each variation is 1-12 on the VARIATION knob.",
  "Beat styles (3-5) play the chord on the rhythm shown. The manual only gives the rhythm, so how the chord is voiced there is not stated.",
  "Style 5 variations 7-12 are 3-step patterns; my reading is that they cycle against the 4-step beat, which is what \"syncopation\" means here (inferred).",
  "The manual does not explain how \"1\" and \"2\" arp variants differ (e.g. Up 1 vs Up 2).",
  "Styles 6-9 have 12 variations each, but the manual only names the style, not each variation."
